```nix
{
  description = "...";

  inputs = {
    nixpkgs.url = "github:NixOS/nixpkgs/nixos-unstable";
    utils.url = "github:numtide/flake-utils";
  };

  outputs = { self, nixpkgs, utils }:
    (utils.lib.eachSystem ["x86_64-linux" ] (system:
      let
        pkgs = import nixpkgs {
          inherit system;
        };
  in rec {
    packages = rec { ... };
    devShell = pkgs.mkShell {
      buildInputs = with pkgs; [ ... ];
      shellHook = ''
        echo "Welcome to the X development environment!"
      '';
    };
  }));
}
```

The most common style (ffcut, tone, tempo-trainer, kyre) uses `utils.lib.eachSystem ["x86_64-linux"]` and `pkgs = import nixpkgs { inherit system; }`. Some use the `flake-utils.lib.eachDefaultSystem` variant.

